  "query_preview": "/Through Monday/...\nIssued at 240 AM MDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nSW flow aloft will remain over the area today with drier air \nspreading across the area.  Thus, will see much lower chances for \nshowers/tstms this aftn. MLCAPE over the far ern plains will range \nfrom 1000-1500 j/kg with bulk shear around 30 kts.  At this time, \ncan't rule out an isold stronger storm or two over the far ern plains\nlate this aftn into the early evening hours.  Over the higher \nterrain only isold to widely sct showers/tstms are expected this \naftn. Highs today will stay near seasonal levels.\n\nFor Wed and Thu, dry air in SW flow aloft will remain over the area \nwith only a slight chc of aftn showers/tstms, mainly over the higher \nterrain.  Temperatures will be warmer as readings rise into the \nupper 80's to lower 90s across the plains.\n\nBy Fri, the flow aloft will become more SSW. Overall, it still looks \nmainly dry with only a slight chc of showers/tstms mainly over the \nhigher terrain.  Highs on Fri will be in the lower to mid 90's \nacross nern CO.\n\nFor the weekend through Labor Day, an upper level high will be over \nthe central US and expand into the srn Rockies, as an upper level\nlow is near the West Coast. As a result, SSW flow aloft will \nremain over the area. Both the ECMWF and GFS show some influx of \nmonsoon moisture beginning on Sat and continuing thru Labor Day. \nThus will keep in a chc of showers/tstms each day over the higher \nterrain with a slight chance across the plains. Temperatures will \nremain above normal thru the period.",
